sec.p:
To check whether the decrease in rate was due to the absolute ATPαS concentration or not, we investigated how the initial apparent mass-action ratio for the ATP synthesis reaction Γ’ = [ATP]/([ADP]∙[Pi]) influences the ATP synthesis rate. At chemical equilibrium, where no net ATP synthesis takes place the mass-action ratio is equal to the equilibrium constant K44. In equilibrium thermodynamics, the Gibbs free energy change is defined by the equation\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
